## Root-Cause Analysis

I compared marketing performance across channels, channel mix, months, and regions to understand what was driving the overall change.

The overall conversion rate increased from 5.71% in 2024 to 5.95% in 2025. The improvement was consistent across all four channels: Email increased from 6.48% to 6.76%, Organic Search from 8.23% to 8.57%, Paid Search from 4.74% to 4.94%, and Paid Social from 3.07% to 3.18%.

I also checked for Simpson's Paradox by comparing the overall result with channel-level performance. The paradox was not present: the overall conversion rate increased and every individual channel also improved. Channel mix remained almost unchanged between the two years, so a major mix-shift does not appear to explain the result.

To check seasonality, I compared each month in 2025 with the same month in 2024 rather than comparing consecutive months. All six months from July through December showed higher conversion rates in 2025.

Regional results also followed a similar pattern without a major regional outlier. Overall, the improvement appears to be broad-based across channels and months rather than being driven by one specific region, channel, or seasonal period.
